claim incense-root-finder-two-shapes
seat incense
stamp 20260917.221017
epoch 1789697417
paths tools/fixtures/r/root_finder_scan.sh
what The fan-out census named root_finder at 895 execve and 615 per mille, and the previous lap measured it alone at 904 processes -- 515 tr, 265 awk, 25 grep, 18 git -- then deliberately left it, because unlike the two files cured before it this one wears TWO shapes rather than one. This lap takes both, separated. SHAPE ONE, the tr: lines 240 to 242 spell the identical subexpression echo dollar-s piped to tr slash underscore THREE times for one value inside the sentinel loop, and line 241 adds a fourth tr stripping spaces from a wc reading. Four spawns an iteration for one derived name and one number. The cure computes the safe name ONCE into a variable, and replaces slashes with POSIX parameter expansion rather than a tool, so the count goes to zero rather than to one. The wc reading loses its tr to word splitting via set --, which strips whitespace with no process at all. SHAPE TWO, the lookup: parents_of spawns awk per call to read one row out of parentmap.txt, and its single call site sits in a NESTED loop -- for each distinct sentinel set, for each sentinel in it. The file's own comment two lines above records that this exact class was already repaired once here, reading the classified table into lists rather than re-awking per sentinel per finder, and names it as most of this scan's wall time; the map lookup survived that pass. The cure reads parentmap once into a variable and walks it in the shell, with IFS saved and restored around the walk. THE PREDICTION IS WRITTEN HERE BEFORE THE BUILD SO IT CAN BE WRONG OUT LOUD: the output stays byte-identical at md5 875b09a1134f02aa4062e59883a1407d over 14 lines with exit 0 unchanged, tr falls to zero, awk falls below 20 from 265, total processes fall below 150 from 904, and the wall falls from its measured 4,109ms by at least half. If the md5 moves the change is withdrawn whole. The comparison runs BOTH versions against the same tree in the same moment, since a baseline captured earlier already gave this lap one false alarm. Touches ONE file; no module source, no ledger row, no roster row, no ceiling any peer watches, and no peer-claimed path -- the check read overlap_peer=0 against three live claims.
